  "body": "Follow-up from review of #364 (gh-361 `file_write` parent-directory fix).\n\n## Problem\n\nJava `FileTools` (epam/dm.ai) normalizes every file-tool path and rejects anything outside the working directory before acting (`resolvedPath.startsWith(workingDir)`, logs `\"Path traversal attempt blocked\"`). The Dart JS-bridge `file_*` family has **no containment check on any tool**:\n\n- `file_write` now creates missing parent directories for any resolved path (gh-361), so absolute paths and `..` segments that escape the job working directory materialize on disk.\n- `file_mkdir` already created arbitrary directory trees.\n- `file_read` / `file_delete` are unbounded the same way.\n\nThis is a pre-existing family-wide gap, **not** a regression introduced by #364 — agent scripts already had equivalent reach via `file_mkdir` + write and via the CLI whitelist. But Java parity (AGENTS.md rule 2) includes the sandbox, and the bridge should match it.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nApply a shared containment check to every `file_*` tool on the synchronous JS-bridge path (`ToolBridge._fileFns`) and the async executor (`FileToolExecutor`), rejecting paths outside the allowed base with the error envelope (or Java's `SecurityException` semantics, rethrown as a JS `Error` on the bridge path — match whatever the rest of the family does).\n\nReusable building blocks already exist: `validateWithinAllowedBase` / `pathIsWithin` / `gitRepositoryRoot` in `lib/src/integrations/cli/allowed_base.dart` implement the exact job-base/git-root/system-tmpdir semantics used by `cli_execute_command` on both the bridge and executor surfaces — file paths should get the same treatment so the two surfaces cannot drift apart again.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every `file_*` bridge tool (`file_read`, `file_write`, `file_write_lines`, `file_append`, `file_list`, `file_exists`, `file_delete`, `file_mkdir`) rejects paths outside the job base / git root / system tmpdir with the standard error envelope.\n- [ ] The async `FileToolExecutor` surface applies the same rule (shared helper, not a copy).\n- [ ] Tests cover: escaping `..` segment, absolute path outside base, legitimate in-base nested path still works (no false rejection), tmpdir paths still allowed.\n- [ ] Java parity decision recorded in the commit message (AGENTS.md rule 2).\n\n## References\n\n- Review thread on #364: \"'Java parity' without Java's sandbox — parent creation now materializes paths outside the working directory\"\n- Java spec: `FileTools.java` in epam/dm.ai (containment check + `\"Path traversal attempt blocked\"`)\n- Dart helpers to reuse: `lib/src/integrations/cli/allowed_base.dart`\n"
}
